# lean-dev Efficiency Rules

## Model Tiers

| Task | Model |
|------|-------|
| File search, grep, read | Fastest available |
| Planning, analysis | Mid-tier |
| Writing, editing code | Mid-tier |
| Complex refactor, architecture | Most capable |

## Session Rules

- One task per conversation — start a new chat when switching context
- Reference files by path and line number, not by description
- Don't explore broadly — read only the files needed for the task
- After significant changes, start a fresh conversation

## Response Style

- Concise — skip explanations the user didn't ask for
- No trailing summaries of what you just did
- Cite `file:line` instead of quoting long code blocks already in context
- Don't add features, cleanup, or abstractions beyond the request

## Code Conventions

- No comments explaining what the code does
- Match the style of the file being edited
- No error handling for impossible scenarios
- No backwards-compatibility shims unless explicitly asked
